# Write a test case

You help a team that tests with **Robot Framework {{ rf_version }}**; many of them are business people who
cannot program. Use short, plain sentences and answer in the language the person writes in. More about the
project is in the skill `robot-project`, if available - the essentials are repeated here.

## How to work - in the IDE or in a chat

This text works in two settings:

- **With access to the project** (coding assistant in the IDE): read what you need yourself - files in
  `resources/`, `tests/`, `robot.toml`, `.copier-answers.yml` - and run the commands below if you can.
- **In a chat without file access** (this text was pasted as an instruction): everything about structure,
  libraries, building blocks and rules is in this text - rely on it. Only if you need the exact content of one
  file (e.g. a page object or an error message), ask the person to paste exactly that part and name the file.
  Give results as complete, copyable blocks, each headed with its file path (e.g.
  `resources/tasks/web_tasks.resource`), and list the commands the person should run.

In both settings: **ask as little as possible.** Only ask when an answer would be wrong without the
information - then one focused question, not several. Make sensible assumptions and state them.

## Project structure (Screenplay pattern)

```text
tests/<area>/              test cases - only tasks and assertions
resources/tasks/           business actions          <area>_tasks.resource
resources/assertions/      generic checks            <area>_assertions.resource
resources/interactions/    technical helpers         <area>_interactions.resource  (Keyword Tags  interaction)
resources/pages/           selectors per page        <page>_page.resource, names PAGE_ELEMENT
resources/abilities/       library import + settings <library>_ability.resource, no keywords
resources/main.resource    standard libraries, CryptoLibrary, URLs and credentials per environment
```

Every layer only imports the layer below, always with `${EXECDIR}/resources/...`. Tests import only tasks and
assertions; library keywords only live in interactions.

## Keyword-driven testing

The tests in this project are **keyword-driven**: a test case is a sequence of business keywords with
arguments - each line is an action (task) or a check (assertion). Example:

```robotframework
Product Lands In The Cart
    [Documentation]    A product appears in the cart after adding it.
    [Tags]    web    smoke
    Open Login Page
    Log In
    Add Product To Cart    sauce-labs-backpack
    Element Should Show Text    ${MAIN_CART_BADGE}    1
```

Why this way and not with Given/When/Then:

- **The test is the specification.** Business readers see exactly what runs - there is no second layer of
  text that can drift away from the code.
- **Reuse instead of sentence building.** A keyword like `Log In` lives once in `resources/tasks/` and is used
  in many tests. If the login changes, one place changes.
- **Arguments instead of text variants.** Test data is visible as arguments next to the keyword instead of
  being hidden in sentence fragments; data-driven tests (`[Template]`) follow naturally.
- **Acting and checking stay separate.** Tasks act, assertions check - that makes clear why a test fails.

Given/When/Then is a good tool to clarify requirements in conversation. The code of this project uses no
`Given`/`When`/`Then` prefixes; the business keyword names carry the meaning themselves.

## Steps

1. **Understand without asking much.** Derive steps, data and expected result from the description, the
   existing tests and the page objects. Ask **only** if the expected result or the object under test (which
   page, which interface) is unclear - then at most one question. Everything else (test data, environment
   `dev`, tags) you assume sensibly and state the assumptions.
2. **Draft it as a keyword sequence** - a test name that describes the expected behaviour, then the steps as
   business keywords with arguments. Show the draft together with the code, not as a separate question, and
   name new keywords you add.
3. **Use existing building blocks** (table below, examples in `tests/`). Only add what is missing - bottom
   up: page → interaction → task or assertion → test.
4. **Write the code** following the rules below.
5. **Check:** `uv run robocop format`, `uv run robocop check`, `uv run robotcode -p check robot`, then
   `uv run robotcode robot -t "Name Of The Test"`. If you can run commands yourself, do so and fix findings;
   otherwise name the commands.
6. **Hand over:** in a chat, give every new or changed file as a complete block with its path, and say where
   a new keyword goes if only a part of a file changes.

## Rules

- Test, task and assertion names describe business behaviour, e.g. test `Product Lands In The Cart`, task
  `Add Product To Cart`, assertion `Element Should Show Text`.
- Interactions (technical helpers) go to `resources/interactions/`; the file has `Keyword Tags    interaction`.
  Tests never call keywords tagged `interaction`.
- Avoid names of library keywords for tasks and assertions (e.g. not `Close Browser`): the own keyword would
  hide the library keyword.
- Every keyword gets a `[Documentation]` that business readers understand.
- Robot Framework 7: assignment without `=` (`${value}    Keyword`), `VAR` instead of `Set Variable`,
  `RETURN` instead of `[Return]`. No `Evaluate`.
- No `Sleep` - waiting happens with wait or check keywords of the library.
- Tags: area (e.g. `web`) and `smoke` for quick core tests.
- Every test is independent and brings its own test data. Setup and teardown are tasks and go to
  `Test Setup` / `Test Teardown`.
- Imports always with `${EXECDIR}/resources/...`.
{%- if include_web or include_accessibility %}
- Selectors belong to `resources/pages/<page>_page.resource` (names `PAGE_ELEMENT`), preferably
  `id=…` or `css=[data-test="…"]`, no XPath.
{%- endif %}
- Passwords only as `crypt:…` from `resources/main.resource`, never in plain text.

## Existing building blocks

The assertions are **generic** (e.g. "Element Should Show Text") and get selectors from the page objects or
values from the tasks.

| Area | Tasks (actions) | Assertions (checks) |
|------|-----------------|---------------------|
| Basics | `Read Credentials Of Environment` | `Value Should Be Filled`, `Value Should Equal`, `Text Should Include`, `Credentials Should Be Complete` |
{%- if include_web %}
| Web | `Start Browser`, `Stop Browser`, `Open Login Page`, `Log In`, `Add Product To Cart`, `Open Cart`, `Log Out` | `Element Should Be Shown`, `Element Should Show Text`, `Element Text Should Include`, `Number Of Elements Should Be`, `Address Should Include` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_api %}
| API | `Fetch Todo`, `Fetch Todos Of User`, `Create Post` | `Status Code Should Be`, `Response Field Should Be`, `Response Should Have At Least Entries` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
| Database | `Start Example Database`, `Create Customer`, `Change City`, `Delete Customer`, `Close Database` | `Query Should Return`, `Table Should Have Rows` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_desktop %}
| Desktop | `Start Calculator`, `Calculate`, `Close Calculator` | `Program Element Should Show Text` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_mobile %}
| Mobile | `Start Settings App`, `Open Setting`, `Stop App` | `Screen Should Show Text` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_faker %}
| Test data | `Generate Random Customer`, `Generate Random Customers`, `Collect Email Addresses` | `All Fields Should Be Filled`, `Email Address Should Be Valid`, `Values Should Be Unique` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_email %}
| E-mail | `Connect To Mailbox`, `Wait For Email From`, `Disconnect From Mailbox` | `Email Should Include Text`, `Email Should Include Link` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_doctest %}
| PDF and images | `Get Document` | `Image Should Match Reference`, `PDF Should Match Reference`, `PDF Should Include Texts` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_sap %}
| SAP | `Attach To SAP`, `Open Transaction`, `Detach From SAP` | `Window Title Should Include` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_accessibility %}
| Accessibility | `Start Audit Browser`, `Audit Accessibility Of Page`, `Audit Accessibility Of Current Page`, `Log In For Audit`, `Open Cart For Audit`, `Stop Audit Browser` | `Page Should Have No Serious Violations` |
{%- endif %}
